    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as our premier engine for offensive production with a commanding score of 81.24. Facing a favorable matchup against Elder (xERA 4.40), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-leverage #2 spot in the lineup, making him the cornerstone of our pursuit of stolen bases and runs. Similarly, **Max Muncy** (71.26) presents significant value against Bradford; despite a lower lineup position, the massive SP skill discrepancy (+19%) and favorable park factors make him a high-upside play. **Josh Naylor** (64.62) and **Gabriel Moreno** (64.15) also project as strong starts, capitalizing on soft opposing rotations to anchor our counting stats. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the roster involves **Jose Caballero** (41.62). While his score is depressed by a tough matchup against Cease and a low batting position, he remains a roster staple purely for his elite speed profile, which we heavily overweight in our 5x5 Roto context. He narrowly edged out **Zach McKinstry** (41.11) for the final outfield slot, as we prioritized **Jose Caballero**'s potential to swing the SB category in tight games, even against a high-tier arm like Cease. Note that **Brice Turang** remains sidelined today, and we are closely monitoring the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure we maintain optimal depth, particularly while key pieces like **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain on the IL. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Austin Riley**, as his late-lineup placement and the proximity to the baseline suggest he is a fringe start unless his BvP metrics shift positively in-game.",
